## Prerequisites

- [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/) v20 or higher
- [Stream Deck](https://www.elgato.com/s/downloads?product=Stream%20Deck) v6.9 or higher
- A Stream Deck device (or [Stream Deck Mobile](https://www.elgato.com/stream-deck-mobile))

## Getting Started

### 1. Install dependencies

```bash
npm install
```

### 2. Start developing

```bash
npm run watch
```

This watches for changes in `src/` and the manifest, rebuilds automatically,
and restarts the plugin in Stream Deck.

### 3. Open Stream Deck

Your plugin should appear in the Stream Deck actions list.  Drag the
**Counter** action onto a key to try it out.

> **Tip:** If your plugin doesn't show up, restart the Stream Deck app. This
> can happen after a fresh install or update.

## Project Structure

```
.
├── {{ plugin_uuid }}.sdPlugin/   # Compiled plugin (distributed to Stream Deck)
│   ├── bin/                       # Rollup build output
│   ├── imgs/                      # Icons & images
│   │   ├── actions/counter/       # Counter action icons
│   │   └── plugin/                # Plugin-level icons
│   ├── ui/                        # Property inspectors (HTML)
│   │   └── counter.html
│   ├── manifest.json              # Plugin manifest (metadata + actions)
│   └── .sdignore                  # Files excluded from packaging
├── src/                           # TypeScript source
│   ├── actions/
│   │   └── counter.ts             # Example counter action
│   └── plugin.ts                  # Entry point — registers actions
├── package.json
├── rollup.config.mjs              # Bundler configuration
├── tsconfig.json                  # TypeScript configuration
└── eslint.config.mjs              # Linter configuration
```

## Available Scripts

| Script            | Description                                              |
| ----------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |
| `npm run build`   | Production build (minified, no source maps)              |
| `npm run watch`   | Dev build with hot-reload and automatic plugin restart   |
| `npm run lint`    | Run ESLint                                               |
| `npm run format`  | Check Prettier formatting                                |
| `npm run pack`    | Package plugin into a `.streamDeckPlugin` installer file |

## Adding a New Action

1. Create a new file in `src/actions/` extending `SingletonAction`.
2. Add the action's metadata to `manifest.json` under `Actions`.
3. Register the action in `src/plugin.ts` before `streamDeck.connect()`.
4. Optionally create a property inspector HTML in `{{ plugin_uuid }}.sdPlugin/ui/`.

See [Actions Guide](https://docs.elgato.com/streamdeck/sdk/guides/actions) for
details.

## Plugin Icons

Replace the placeholder `.gitkeep` files in the `imgs/` directories with your
actual icons:

| Path                            | Size          | Purpose                       |
| ------------------------------- | ------------- | ----------------------------- |
| `imgs/plugin/marketplace`       | 288 × 288 px  | Marketplace listing           |
| `imgs/plugin/category-icon`     | 28 × 28 px    | Category in actions list      |
| `imgs/actions/counter/icon`     | 20 × 20 px    | Action icon in actions list   |
| `imgs/actions/counter/key`      | 72 × 72 px    | Default key image             |

> File extensions must be **omitted** for `Icon`, `CategoryIcon`, and `Image`
> paths in `manifest.json`. Stream Deck resolves `@1x` / `@2x` variants
> automatically.

## Debugging

1. Start `npm run watch`.
2. In VS Code press **F5** → select *Attach to Stream Deck Plugin*.
3. Choose the `node20` (or `node24`) process.

Property inspector debugging is available at <http://localhost:23654/> when
developer mode is enabled (`streamdeck dev`).

## Distribution

```bash
npm run pack
```

This creates a `.streamDeckPlugin` file you can distribute directly or upload to
[Maker Console](https://maker.elgato.com/) for Marketplace publication.

See [Distribution Guide](https://docs.elgato.com/streamdeck/sdk/introduction/distribution)
for more details.

